sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The constant angle of the logarithmic spiral is about 80° in Nautilus, where each whorl is about three times as broad as its predecessor, and in ordinary ammonitoid and typical spiral gastropod shells is seldom below 80° and usually between 80° and 85°.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The constant angle of nautiloid, ammonitoid and gastropod spirals is about 80°–85°";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "\\alpha \\approx 80^\\circ in Nautilus (b_{n+1}/b_n \\approx 3); usually 80^\\circ \\le \\alpha \\le 85^\\circ in ammonitoid and gastropod shells";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XI, “The Logarithmic Spiral”; topic “Constant angle of molluscan spirals”. Scope: Nautilus, ammonoids and spiral gastropods"
}
